    "body": "I did some more digging into this and think I know what's going on (because I see it too).\r\n\r\nThe region you're seeing is coming from your ~/.aws/config file because you have a `[default]` profile and region configured. [This line](https://github.com/starship/starship/blob/master/src/modules/aws.rs#L53) (I think) is looking for your default profile and then looking for the region you have configured.\r\n\r\nI have this in my config file and I always have us-west-2 shown even when I don't have an `AWS_REGION` environment variable set.\r\n```\r\n[default]\r\noutput = json\r\nregion = us-west-2\r\ntcp_keepalive = true\r\n```\r\nI confirmed it was looking at this file because when I change that value the starship value changes too.\r\n\r\nSo in order to fix this annoyance I removed the region from my default profile and I added it explicitly to each profile.",
